course: dictionary
lesson: 13407
title: Heroic and the clues around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Heroic comes from hero, a person who is very brave or does something great. Heroic tells you that someone acts like a hero. The words around it are its context, and they show you which kind of heroic is meant.
explain: «The firefighter made a heroic rescue and carried the boy out of the burning house.» The clues are rescue, burning house and carried the boy out, so heroic means very brave and helpful in danger. Test it by swapping in your meaning: «The firefighter made a very brave rescue» still makes sense.
explain: Heroic can also describe a great effort, with no danger at all. «Mia made a heroic effort to finish her long project.» Nobody was in danger; heroic shows how hard she worked. Heroic can also mean to do with heroes in old stories, such as «the heroic legends of Hercules».
explain: Watch out for heroics, a noun. «Jay's heroics on his bike nearly got him hurt.» Heroics means showing off brave actions, often foolishly. Being heroic does not mean taking silly risks: a real hero gets help first.
fact: Heroic means very brave, like a hero.
fact: «Heroic» can also mean to do with heroes in old stories and poems.
fact: «Heroic» can mean very great or large in effort, as in «a heroic effort».
fact: Heroics (noun) means showing off brave actions, sometimes foolishly.
fact: The adverb «heroically» means in a brave way: «The crew heroically rowed through the storm to reach the ship.»
exercise: «The lifeboat crew made a heroic rescue in the storm.» What does heroic mean here? | Very wet from the rain | Very slow and lazy | Very quiet | *Very brave and helpful
exercise: «Sam made a heroic effort to finish the race, even though his legs ached.» What does heroic show about the effort? | It was short and easy | It was done by a robot | *It was very great and hard work | It was done in the dark
exercise: Ben jumped off the wall to show off, and his teacher said his heroics were silly. What are heroics? | *Showing off brave actions, sometimes foolishly | Heroes from old stories | Quiet, careful walks | Very large meals
test: «The old poem told heroic legends of brave knights.» What does heroic mean here? | Very sleepy | Very cold and wet | *To do with heroes in old stories and poems | Brand new
test: «Lara said, "Stay back, get help first, and do not try to be heroic by climbing the cliff."» What does heroic suggest? | *Taking a silly, dangerous risk to show off | Very quiet and careful | Sad and tired | Very tidy
exam: Which word fits the gap? «The fireman acted ___ to save the cat from the tree.» | heroics | heroic | *heroically | heroes
